hyperlite — IMC-DDMC Radiation Transport for Interacting Transients
===================================================================

A modernized fork of SuperLite (Wagle et al. 2023, ApJ 953 132), a 1-D
spherical multi-group Implicit Monte Carlo / Discrete Diffusion Monte
Carlo radiation-transport code for spectral synthesis of interacting
supernovae, descended from the LANL/UW-Madison SuperNu code.

Documentation: docs/ (built with mkdocs; see docs/index.md).
Changes vs SuperLite 1.x: CHANGELOG.md. Modernization plan: OVERHAUL.md.

Quickstart
----------
Requires CMake >= 3.23, gfortran >= 10, LAPACK/BLAS, HDF5 (Fortran),
Python 3 + numpy/h5py; optional OpenMPI.

    cmake --preset gfortran-openmp        # or gfortran-serial / -mpi / -debug
    cmake --build --preset gfortran-openmp -j
    ctest --preset gfortran-openmp        # unit + smoke + statistical regression

Stage and run a case:

    mkdir run && cd run
    ln -s ../data/* . && ln -s ../tests/cases/w7/* .
    ln -sf input_w7.str input.str && cp input.par.lte input.par
    ../build/gfortran-openmp/superlite

Runs write a self-describing output.h5 (plus legacy ASCII tables while
in_io_ascii = t). Atomic data is read from data/atomic.h5, generated at
build time. OpenMP is on by default (in_nomp = 0 = all threads) and
results are independent of thread count (counter-based Philox RNG).

Highlights of the fork
----------------------
- Modern CMake + CTest + CI (gfortran serial/OpenMP/MPI, ifx); F2018,
  -Wall clean.
- 5.4x faster on the reference case (SoA particles, per-cell DDMC
  tables, threading by default).
- Statistical regression suite with a committed 20-seed reference
  ensemble; unit tests; benchmark harness.
- HDF5 primary I/O; no more Atoms/ CWD dependency.
- Physics fixes: LTE partition-function caching (results previously
  depended on MPI rank count; L_tot +15% on W7), stale DDMC Doppler
  cache. See CHANGELOG.md and docs/migration.md.
- Python tools packaged as hyperlite-tools (pip install -e tools/).

Citing
------
If you use this code, please cite the SuperLite method paper
(Gururaj A. Wagle et al 2023 ApJ 953 132, doi:10.3847/1538-4357/acda23)
and the SuperLite Zenodo record (10.5281/zenodo.8102236). See
CITATION.cff.

